  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n0.4 = 0.4444...\n\n0.2 = 0.2222...\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n1. Convert 0.4 to a Fraction\n\n⇒ Let x = 0.4.\n\n⇒ 10x = 4.4\n\n⇒ 10x - x = 4.4 - 0.4\n\n⇒ 9x = 4\n\n⇒ x = 4/9\n\nSo, 0.4 = 4/9.\n\n2. Convert 0.2 to a Fraction\n\n⇒ Let y = 0.2.\n\n⇒ 10y = 2.2\n\n⇒ 10y - y = 2.2 - 0.2\n\n⇒ 9y = 2\n\n⇒ y = 2/9\n\nSo, 0.2 = 2/9.\n\n3. Add the Two Fractions\n\n⇒ 0.4 + 0.2 = 4/9 + 2/9 = (4 + 2)/9 = 6/9 = 2/3\n\n**∴ The value of 0.4 + 0.2 is 2/3.**",
